<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mazandaran</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mazandaran is a province on the southern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. Its humid lowlands produced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a>, which was a major export of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> took a particular interest in the province and its silk production.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mazandaran.jpg" alt="Mazandaran" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Safa.daneshvar · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:030915-Damavand-Polour-IMG_3449-4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
